<!--
  AbxrLib world-space objects: IL2CPP managed-code-stripping preservation.

  The MonoBehaviours on the keyboard, PIN pad, exit-poll, and QR-scan prefabs are only ever
  reached through those serialized assets, never from code, so IL2CPP with managed stripping at
  Medium or higher prunes them. In a player that shows up as "The referenced script ... is
  missing!" and sign-in UI that instantiates as blank panels.

  This reproduces on Unity 2021.3; Unity 6 auto-preserves asset-referenced types, which masks it.
  Preserving both assemblies keeps every type regardless of the project's Managed Stripping Level.

  This file ships with the sample rather than with the core package: once imported, these
  assemblies are compiled from the project's own Assets folder, so core's link.xml no longer
  covers them.
-->
<linker>
  <assembly fullname="AbxrLib.WorldSpace" preserve="all" />
  <assembly fullname="AbxrLib.UiRoundedCorners" preserve="all" />
</linker>
